"""Give a dataset somewhere to record which source said it exists.

A dataset has been single-sourced until now: the writer catalogue creates it
and every sync overwrites every field of it. Once a centre's own discovery
metadata is read as well, one of the two payloads has to lose the canonical
record, and there is nowhere to put the disagreement -- which is the whole of
what a divergence report would be about.

``DatasetSource`` is the same shape ``StationSource`` already has for stations:
one declaration row per source beside one canonical dataset, each carrying what
that source said and when it was first and last heard saying it. Nothing about
the dataset itself changes, and the operator's expected interval stays where it
is, on the canonical record, belonging to none of the sources.

The sync log alteration carried along with it changes no column: it is a help
text that had drifted from the model, and taking it here is cheaper than
leaving ``makemigrations`` to offer it again on every run.
"""

